.Sh DESCRIPTION
These routines set and get the holder identity of an X509 attribute
certificate.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_set0_holder_entityName
sets the identity as a
.Sy GENERAL_NAME
.Fa name ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_set0_holder_baseCertId
sets the identity based on the issuer and serial number of a certificate
detailed in
.Fa isss
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_set0_holder_digest
sets the holder entity based on digest information
.Fa dinfo .
Although RFC 5755 section 4.2.2 recommends that only one of the above
methods be used to set the holder identity for a given attribute
certificate
.Fa x ,
setting multiple methods at the same time is possible.
It is up to the application to handle cases when conflicting identity
information is specified using different methods.
.Pp
Pointers to the internal structures describing the holder identity of
attribute certificate
.Fa x
can be retrieved with
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_holder_entityName ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_holder_baseCertId ,
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_holder_digest .
.Pp
A
.Vt OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL
object holds the subject name and UID of a certificate issuer and a
certificate's serial number.
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_set1_issuer ,
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_set1_issuerUID ,
and
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_set1_serial
respectively copy these values into the
.Vt OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL
structure.
The application is responsible for freeing its own copy of these values
after use.
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_get0_issuer ,
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_get0_issuerUID ,
and
.Fn OSSL_ISSUER_SERIAL_get0_serial
return pointers to these values in the object.
.Pp
An
.Vt OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO
object holds a digest of data to identify the attribute certificate
holder.
.Fn OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO_set1_digest
sets the digest information of the object.
The type of
.Fa digest
information is given by
.Fa digestedObjectType
and can be one of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO_PUBLIC_KEY
Hash of a public key
.It OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO_PUBLIC_KEY_CERT
Hash of a public key certificate
.It OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO_OTHER
Hash of another object.
See NOTES below.
.El
.Pp
.Fa digestAlgorithm
indicates the algorithm used to compute
.Fa digest .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All
.Em set0 Ns / Ns Em set1
routines return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
All
.Em get0
functions return a pointer to the object's inner structure.
These pointers must not be freed after use.
.Sh NOTES
Although the value of
.Sy OSSL_OBJECT_DIGEST_INFO_OTHER
is defined in RFC 5755, its use is prohibited for conformant attribute
certificates.
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
